[Music]  finally tonight there's an opening on  the supreme court and the confirmation  process has certainly changed over the  years antonin scalia was confirmed 98-0  ruth bader ginsburg 96-3 anthony kennedy  97-0 stephen breyer 87-9 even john  roberts was confirmed 78-22  but that's when things began to change  because of who was in the group voting  no joe biden voted no and barack obama  voted no and so did hillary clinton and  dick durbin and chuck schumer and john  kerry the last four democrat nominees  for president voted no  john roberts was unanimously rated well  qualified by the american bar  association not a single dissenting vote  but that wasn't enough for these four  future democrat nominees for president  they opposed john roberts because it was  politically expedient to do so  being fair was hardly a match for their  political ambition  here we go again with biden's first  opening on the high court he says he  wants a supreme court that looks like  america  if that's true it's a brand new position  for him in 1991 joe biden was in the  senate when thurgood marshall retired  from the supreme court and clarence  thomas was nominated to fill vacancy  clarence thomas is black he would have  replaced the only black supreme court  justice  in a country where 13 percent of the  population was black  but joe biden voted no if biden had his  way the supreme court would have been  all white  and that doesn't look like america  joe biden now says he wants a black  female on the high court but he opposed  a black female in 2005. even worse he  used that old jim crow relic called a  filibuster  to try and keep judge janice rogers  brown off the d.c court of appeals and  biden made it clear he would use the  filibuster again  if she were ever nominated for the  supreme court in fact biden quoted  senator robert byrd while he was  opposing a black woman for the highest  echelons of our judiciary  ain't that some irony quoting a former  klansman while you oppose a black  nominee  that doesn't look like america and then  there's miguel estrada in 2001 estrada  who was hispanic was nominated for the  d.c court of appeals he was found well  qualified by the american bar  association but biden and other senate  democrats blocked him  in 2001 13 percent of the country was  hispanic and exactly zero members of the  supreme court were  biden and the democrats did not just  keep a hispanic man off the second  highest court in the country they kept  him off the bench because he was  hispanic  and this from the crowd who now claims  they want the judiciary to look like  america president biden may want the  court to look like america but senator  biden most assuredly  did not  i can't think of anything that looks  more like america than being a mother  while you also excel in your profession  mothers have been balancing work and  home since the dawn of time  if you really want something to look  like america every single one of us was  brought into the world  by a mother  so what could possibly look more like  america than putting a mother on the  high court especially one rated well  qualified by the american bar  association  sandra day o'connor and ruth bader  ginsburg were both mothers but neither  was on the bench in 2020 when amy coney  barrett was nominated  you claim you want the court to look  like america there are 85 million  mothers in this country and not a single  one on the supreme court at that time so  why did every single senate democrat  oppose putting what would have been the  only mother  on the supreme court  joe biden had a chance to make the court  look like america but he refused  he opposed a black man a black woman a  hispanic man and a mother  and all were qualified all would have  made the court more diverse but biden  said no  and now joe biden has promised to make  the next supreme court justice a black  female  americans including a majority of  democrats believe biden should consider  all nominees  so why not look for the most qualified  candidates period mr president  i am fully convinced some of the names  on that list would be black women i can  think of several right now one would be  michelle chiles from south carolina she  can compete no matter the pool of  applicants  the people who know her and work with  her and appear before her  are universal in their praise for her  character and her intelligence and her  work ethic and to meet her she was  elected to a state court judgeship in  south carolina a state hardly known for  quotas or affirmative action  she was elected out of all the  candidates because she was the most  qualified not because she was a black  woman  she was elected by a  republican-dominated legislature another  entity not known for its embrace of  quotas or affirmative action or set  asides  she was later confirmed by a voice vote  by the u.s senate for a federal  judgeship not one single senator opposed  her  among those supporting her included  former senator jim demint who some  consider to be the grandfather of the  tea party movement  i don't think it was quotas or a belief  in affirmative action that motivated  senator dement to support judge michelle  chiles  she was nominated and confirmed because  she was supremely qualified  and this has been borne out by her time  on the federal bench there's a  difference between picking someone who  is supremely qualified and happens to be  black and picking someone because she is  black  all biden had to do was say he was going  to find the most qualified person for  the job period that list would have  undoubtedly included black women and he  could have picked one of those black  women but he didn't do that he wanted to  make a political point he wanted to help  himself and in the process he sent the  wrong message  black women do not need to compete  merely among themselves for one to  prevail they can and should and do  prevail no matter the competition and i  have seen it countless times you should  look for it yourself  joe biden now claims he wants a court  that looks like  america despite the fact that he whiffed  when he could have done that in the past  and in the process he has refused to do  the one thing that looks the very most  like america  pick the most qualified person  i have every confidence that would have  been a black woman  i wish you did too mr president  i'm steve ducey i'm brian kill me and  i'm ainslie earhart and click here to  subscribe to the fox news youtube page  to catch our hottest interviews and most  compelling analysis

